 - Calls to `load_file` will be recorded on the inspect history and include module and line number.
 
+**new in 3.2.11**
+
+- You can bypass environment filtering by passing `env=False` to `load_file`. This loads all top-level variables directly from the file without applying any environment-specific logic or layers. Useful for loading environment-agnostic files.
+
+```python
+# Load file without environment filtering
+settings.load_file(path="/path/to/file.toml", env=False)
+```
 
